{
  "video": {
    "id": "sAD1Xr3-rmI",
    "title": "Basic Mechanisms of Cloning, excerpt 3 | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sAD1Xr3-rmI",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 850,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 294,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 7.06,
      "end": 8.54,
      "duration": 1.48,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: So now I have this."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.54,
      "end": 12.066,
      "duration": 3.526,
      "text": "And what I need to do is I need to transform."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 17.79,
      "end": 28.2,
      "duration": 10.41,
      "text": "So I need to take E.coli growing in a test tube."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 28.2,
      "end": 34.51,
      "duration": 6.31,
      "text": "And I need to put into it a whole collection of zillions"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 34.51,
      "end": 40.71,
      "duration": 6.2,
      "text": "and zillions of plasmid molecules, plasmid circles"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 40.71,
      "end": 44.07,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "that all have different pieces of human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 44.07,
      "end": 46.26,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "One of these things might have ARG1, one ARG2,"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 46.26,
      "end": 48.63,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "one ARG3, et cetera."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 48.63,
      "end": 50.68,
      "duration": 2.05,
      "text": "Or if it's human DNA, one of them your hemoglobin, one of"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 50.68,
      "end": 52.42,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "them your collagen, whatever."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 52.42,
      "end": 55.39,
      "duration": 2.97,
      "text": "I have to throw the DNA on top of the bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 59.41,
      "end": 62.21,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "And then I need to come up with some engineering trick to"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 62.21,
      "end": 68.57,
      "duration": 6.36,
      "text": "make the bacteria take up this DNA across their cell"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 68.57,
      "end": 73.63,
      "duration": 5.06,
      "text": "membranes and use it."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 73.63,
      "end": 76.46,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "Why should I be able to persuade bacteria"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 76.46,
      "end": 79.656,
      "duration": 3.196,
      "text": "to take up my DNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 79.656,
      "end": 80.62,
      "duration": 0.964,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: They do it anyway."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 80.62,
      "end": 81.57,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: They do it anyway."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 81.57,
      "end": 83.55,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "Remember, we said they like to exchange DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 83.55,
      "end": 85.71,
      "duration": 2.16,
      "text": "That's kind of their thing, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 85.71,
      "end": 89.06,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "They pick up DNA from their environment anyway."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 89.06,
      "end": 92.44,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "See, as usual, we haven't really invented something."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 92.44,
      "end": 95.78,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "What we've done is we have used the natural property"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 95.78,
      "end": 96.97,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "that's out there."
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 96.97,
      "end": 100.69,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "The natural properties, bacteria like to slurp up DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 100.69,
      "end": 104.52,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "Now in fairness, some pretty cool protocols were developed"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 104.52,
      "end": 107.05,
      "duration": 2.53,
      "text": "that improve the ability to do it."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 107.05,
      "end": 109.29,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "You treat the DNA, a little nastily."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 109.29,
      "end": 110.72,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "You give it certain ions."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 110.72,
      "end": 112.64,
      "duration": 1.92,
      "text": "You heat shock it in a certain way."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 112.64,
      "end": 116.42,
      "duration": 3.78,
      "text": "And then it encourages it to slurp up DNA better."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 116.42,
      "end": 118.41,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "But the ability to slurp up DNA was there"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 118.41,
      "end": 119.58,
      "duration": 1.17,
      "text": "in the first place."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 119.58,
      "end": 122.63,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "We couldn't have given it the ability to slurp up DNA if it"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 122.63,
      "end": 123.2,
      "duration": 0.57,
      "text": "wasn't there."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 123.2,
      "end": 126.84,
      "duration": 3.64,
      "text": "But we can always goose it up, improve it in certain ways."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 126.84,
      "end": 129.5,
      "duration": 2.66,
      "text": "And there are great protocols that were developed in order"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 129.5,
      "end": 133.51,
      "duration": 4.01,
      "text": "to be able to increase the efficiency of such"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 133.51,
      "end": 135.15,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "transformation."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 135.15,
      "end": 140.67,
      "duration": 5.52,
      "text": "So now we now have our E.coli."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 140.67,
      "end": 143.8,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "Here's an E.coli."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 143.8,
      "end": 152.16,
      "duration": 8.36,
      "text": "Some of the E.coli have acquired a plasmid containing"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 152.16,
      "end": 155.13,
      "duration": 2.97,
      "text": "human DNA or maybe, if we used yeast, yeast DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 160.75,
      "end": 161.89,
      "duration": 1.14,
      "text": "Some of them have it, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 161.89,
      "end": 163.55,
      "duration": 1.66,
      "text": "Because it's kind of a random process."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 163.55,
      "end": 165.91,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "Some slurp it up, some haven't."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 165.91,
      "end": 170.24,
      "duration": 4.33,
      "text": "So I might have, I don't know, maybe one in 100 of my cells"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 170.24,
      "end": 171.52,
      "duration": 1.28,
      "text": "will have slurped up DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 171.52,
      "end": 176.5,
      "duration": 4.98,
      "text": "But 99 in 100 won't have slurped up DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 176.5,
      "end": 181.53,
      "duration": 5.03,
      "text": "I want to plate these out on a Petri plate and grow them up"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 181.53,
      "end": 184.71,
      "duration": 3.18,
      "text": "into individual colonies."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 184.71,
      "end": 187.0,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "But I would like it to be the case, please, that the"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 187.0,
      "end": 189.75,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "individual colonies that grow up are only the ones that got"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 189.75,
      "end": 191.19,
      "duration": 1.44,
      "text": "my plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 191.19,
      "end": 192.84,
      "duration": 1.65,
      "text": "I really don't want to see all these guys who"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 192.84,
      "end": 196.21,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "didn't get my plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 196.21,
      "end": 196.98,
      "duration": 0.77,
      "text": "So what do I do?"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 196.98,
      "end": 200.63,
      "duration": 3.65,
      "text": "Do I go in there with a microscope and try to figure"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 200.63,
      "end": 203.528,
      "duration": 2.898,
      "text": "out which ones got my human DNA plasmid?"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 207.69,
      "end": 211.41,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "So I would love to plate it out and only have the guys who"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 211.41,
      "end": 212.66,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "got my plasmid grow."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 215.48,
      "end": 218.03,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "How do I arrange that only the guys who got my"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 218.03,
      "end": 219.28,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "plasmid will grow?"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 222.24,
      "end": 223.06,
      "duration": 0.82,
      "text": "Sorry?"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 223.06,
      "end": 225.25,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 225.25,
      "end": 225.86,
      "duration": 0.61,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: For something."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 225.86,
      "end": 229.16,
      "duration": 3.3,
      "text": "I got to put in a gene into that plasmid so that only the"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 229.16,
      "end": 231.53,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "guys who get that will grow."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 231.53,
      "end": 235.086,
      "duration": 3.556,
      "text": "Any ideas for what gene might go in there?"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 235.086,
      "end": 237.0,
      "duration": 1.914,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 237.0,
      "end": 237.746,
      "duration": 0.746,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Sorry?"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 237.746,
      "end": 239.81,
      "duration": 2.064,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 239.81,
      "end": 242.42,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: How about a gene conferring resistance to an"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 242.42,
      "end": 244.41,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "antibiotic."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 244.41,
      "end": 246.27,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "And then what could I do?"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 246.27,
      "end": 247.52,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Well, I could plate."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 252.73,
      "end": 253.98,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "I'm going to select--"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 258.459,
      "end": 261.29,
      "duration": 2.831,
      "text": "see this E.coli here, it had my plasmid."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 261.29,
      "end": 263.15,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "And it's going to have a drug resistance gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 263.15,
      "end": 265.08,
      "duration": 1.93,
      "text": "And it will grow up."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 265.08,
      "end": 268.565,
      "duration": 3.485,
      "text": "This guy over here, he didn't get a drug resistance gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 268.565,
      "end": 270.36,
      "duration": 1.795,
      "text": "He doesn't grow up."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 270.36,
      "end": 274.78,
      "duration": 4.42,
      "text": "The only ones who grow up have a drug resistant--"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 274.78,
      "end": 277.95,
      "duration": 3.17,
      "text": "wait a second."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 277.95,
      "end": 279.617,
      "duration": 1.667,
      "text": "Why doesn't this guy grow up?"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 284.09,
      "end": 285.09,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: You add the drug."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 285.09,
      "end": 288.17,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Oh, I got to add the drug, good point."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 288.17,
      "end": 291.11,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "So what I'm going to do is I add my drug to the plate."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 293.64,
      "end": 298.96,
      "duration": 5.32,
      "text": "I add my drug to the medium, to the Petri plate here."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 298.96,
      "end": 302.17,
      "duration": 3.21,
      "text": "And now my Petri plate is say a penicillin plate or a"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 302.17,
      "end": 304.74,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "streptomycin plate or a ampicillin plate or a"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 304.74,
      "end": 307.15,
      "duration": 2.41,
      "text": "kanamycin plate or whatever."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 307.15,
      "end": 310.3,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "And then the only things that could grow up are the ones"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 310.3,
      "end": 313.11,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "that have resistance to whatever antibiotic I used."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 313.11,
      "end": 315.58,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "So I grow them up on that plate."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 315.58,
      "end": 317.91,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "And they grew up just fine."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 317.91,
      "end": 321.96,
      "duration": 4.05,
      "text": "The ones who didn't get-- now how did I get that antibiotic"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 321.96,
      "end": 323.238,
      "duration": 1.278,
      "text": "gene into the plasmid?"
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 326.99,
      "end": 329.89,
      "duration": 2.9,
      "text": "It actually comes that way in nature, sort of."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 329.89,
      "end": 331.05,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "Now when I get good, I can move them"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 331.05,
      "end": 332.43,
      "duration": 1.38,
      "text": "around from one to another."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 332.43,
      "end": 336.31,
      "duration": 3.88,
      "text": "But nature thought of it first."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 336.31,
      "end": 338.63,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "Nature gave us something that had an origin of replication"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 338.63,
      "end": 341.06,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "and an antibiotic resistance gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 341.06,
      "end": 342.84,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "And we could just add things to it."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 342.84,
      "end": 344.64,
      "duration": 1.8,
      "text": "It had everything we needed."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 344.64,
      "end": 346.39,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "It had the ability to slurp up DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 346.39,
      "end": 350.73,
      "duration": 4.34,
      "text": "It had the ability to confer a new property on the cells like"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 350.73,
      "end": 352.37,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "resistance to antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 352.37,
      "end": 356.51,
      "duration": 4.14,
      "text": "And when we're done, we have a library here."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 362.07,
      "end": 371.42,
      "duration": 9.35,
      "text": "And we call this a library of cells or colonies, each one of"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 371.42,
      "end": 375.04,
      "duration": 3.62,
      "text": "which has a distinct piece of human DNA, each one of which"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 375.04,
      "end": 376.6,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "has a different piece of human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 380.987,
      "end": 383.19,
      "duration": 2.203,
      "text": "Let me stop and ask, any questions?"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 383.19,
      "end": 385.04,
      "duration": 1.85,
      "text": "This is like one of the coolest"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 385.04,
      "end": 386.83,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "new procedures invented."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 386.83,
      "end": 387.83,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "Yes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 387.83,
      "end": 389.763,
      "duration": 1.933,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Is it possible that the same E.coli takes in two"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 389.763,
      "end": 391.47,
      "duration": 1.707,
      "text": "of the things?"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 391.47,
      "end": 396.75,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Is it possible that same E.coli takes in two?"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 396.75,
      "end": 402.0,
      "duration": 5.25,
      "text": "Yes, turns out we do this at a dilution in a way so that most"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 402.0,
      "end": 407.17,
      "duration": 5.17,
      "text": "take up zero, some take up one, and a couple take up two."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 407.17,
      "end": 410.96,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "And what we say there is, oh well."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 410.96,
      "end": 411.99,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "It's not so common."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 411.99,
      "end": 413.59,
      "duration": 1.6,
      "text": "And we live with it."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 413.59,
      "end": 415.158,
      "duration": 1.568,
      "text": "What else?"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 415.158,
      "end": 418.152,
      "duration": 2.994,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: You need to make sure the bacteria that doesn't"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 418.152,
      "end": 419.65,
      "duration": 1.498,
      "text": "already have a resistance to it?"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 419.65,
      "end": 421.99,
      "duration": 2.34,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: I better use a bacteria that's not already"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 421.99,
      "end": 425.75,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "resistant to this antibiotic, good point."
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 425.75,
      "end": 426.49,
      "duration": 0.74,
      "text": "That's right."
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 426.49,
      "end": 427.04,
      "duration": 0.55,
      "text": "And I can do that."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 427.04,
      "end": 427.993,
      "duration": 0.953,
      "text": "Yes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 427.993,
      "end": 429.965,
      "duration": 1.972,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: When making those vectors, how do you make sure"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 429.965,
      "end": 433.662,
      "duration": 3.697,
      "text": "it only cuts once so you can put one piece of human DNA and"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 433.662,
      "end": 434.895,
      "duration": 1.233,
      "text": "it doesn't break apart?"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 434.895,
      "end": 440.79,
      "duration": 5.895,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Oh, so what if the vector had five EcoR1 sites?"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 440.79,
      "end": 444.17,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "People have engineered them to just have one."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 444.17,
      "end": 447.5,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "In fact, what they've really done now is they engineer them"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 447.5,
      "end": 450.26,
      "duration": 2.76,
      "text": "so that within the vector there's a little region,"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 450.26,
      "end": 454.37,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "called a polylinker, that has many different sites for many"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 454.37,
      "end": 456.47,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "text": "different restriction enzymes, depending on which one you"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 456.47,
      "end": 457.17,
      "duration": 0.7,
      "text": "might want to use."
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 457.17,
      "end": 459.13,
      "duration": 1.96,
      "text": "And they're all right over here in the same place."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 459.13,
      "end": 461.67,
      "duration": 2.54,
      "text": "And they go around and they fix the vector."
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 461.67,
      "end": 463.73,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "So it doesn't have any of the others."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 463.73,
      "end": 466.74,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "You could, for example cut it open and change the sequence a"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 466.74,
      "end": 467.04,
      "duration": 0.3,
      "text": "little bit."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 467.04,
      "end": 468.81,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "All these tools are available to us."
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 468.81,
      "end": 470.51,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "And rather than you having to do it,"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 470.51,
      "end": 471.59,
      "duration": 1.08,
      "text": "they're all in the catalog."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 471.59,
      "end": 474.3,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "The catalog has vectors that have polylinkers, don't have"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 474.3,
      "end": 475.65,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "any other cut sites, et cetera."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 475.65,
      "end": 477.132,
      "duration": 1.482,
      "text": "Yes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 477.132,
      "end": 480.604,
      "duration": 3.472,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: How do you isolate the sequence you want if the"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 480.604,
      "end": 483.09,
      "duration": 2.486,
      "text": "cutting sequence is so frequent?"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 483.09,
      "end": 486.21,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Oh, so you're asking two questions."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 486.21,
      "end": 490.29,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "One is you're asking how do I find the particular thing I'm"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 490.29,
      "end": 492.39,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "text": "looking for on the plate amongst the millions of"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 492.39,
      "end": 494.08,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "colonies that might grow up?"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 494.08,
      "end": 496.32,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "Or are you asking if the cutting sequence is so"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 496.32,
      "end": 499.77,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "frequent, how do I avoid cutting in the middle of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 499.77,
      "end": 501.02,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "sequence I want?"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 505.6,
      "end": 505.945,
      "duration": 0.345,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Well both, I guess."
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 505.945,
      "end": 510.47,
      "duration": 4.525,
      "text": "If you want to replicate human genes, if you have a bunch of"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 510.47,
      "end": 512.905,
      "duration": 2.435,
      "text": "DNA, how can you make it so that you"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 512.905,
      "end": 515.83,
      "duration": 2.925,
      "text": "isolate only that gene?"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 515.83,
      "end": 517.53,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: OK, so now there are really two questions"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 517.53,
      "end": 518.12,
      "duration": 0.59,
      "text": "you're asking."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 518.12,
      "end": 520.22,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "text": "They're both really good questions."
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 520.22,
      "end": 525.53,
      "duration": 5.31,
      "text": "One, I take my human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 525.53,
      "end": 529.97,
      "duration": 4.44,
      "text": "And let's say we're trying to clone the gene for"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 529.97,
      "end": 531.68,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 531.68,
      "end": 533.89,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "Beta-globin is a part of hemoglobin."
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 533.89,
      "end": 538.28,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "It's one of the two proteins in hemoglobin."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 538.28,
      "end": 546.71,
      "duration": 8.43,
      "text": "And let's say the beta-globin gene is a certain length."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 546.71,
      "end": 552.82,
      "duration": 6.11,
      "text": "And suppose the beta-globin gene actually has several"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 552.82,
      "end": 554.07,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "EcoR1 sites."
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 560.48,
      "end": 562.38,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "I'm going to chop it up into multiple pieces."
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 562.38,
      "end": 564.25,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "That's bad, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 564.25,
      "end": 567.37,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "That's step one bad."
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 567.37,
      "end": 568.62,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "How do I avoid that?"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 571.24,
      "end": 572.13,
      "duration": 0.89,
      "text": "Sorry?"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 572.13,
      "end": 573.54,
      "duration": 1.41,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Paste it."
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 573.54,
      "end": 574.16,
      "duration": 0.62,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Paste it again."
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 574.16,
      "end": 576.96,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "Oh no, once I cut it, all the pieces of human DNA are"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 576.96,
      "end": 577.7,
      "duration": 0.74,
      "text": "floating around."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 577.7,
      "end": 580.09,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "How do I know what to paste to what?"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 580.09,
      "end": 581.47,
      "duration": 1.38,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Methylate it."
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 581.47,
      "end": 582.63,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Methylate it."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 582.63,
      "end": 584.8,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "So first I could take my human DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 584.8,
      "end": 586.47,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "And I could methylate it."
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 586.47,
      "end": 588.03,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "Then it won't get cut up by the enzyme."
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 588.03,
      "end": 590.12,
      "duration": 2.09,
      "text": "But what's the problem with that?"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 590.12,
      "end": 591.64,
      "duration": 1.52,
      "text": "None of it will get cut up with the enzyme."
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 595.23,
      "end": 598.62,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "Suppose I did something that was a compromise though."
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 598.62,
      "end": 605.89,
      "duration": 7.27,
      "text": "Suppose I added a little methylase and a little"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 605.89,
      "end": 608.18,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "restriction enzyme."
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 608.18,
      "end": 611.7,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "And the methylase went around randomly and put some"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 611.7,
      "end": 614.02,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "methyl groups on."
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 614.02,
      "end": 616.64,
      "duration": 2.62,
      "text": "Then these wouldn't get cut."
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 616.64,
      "end": 620.62,
      "duration": 3.98,
      "text": "And sometimes it might put on that."
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 620.62,
      "end": 622.01,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "And those wouldn't get cut."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 622.01,
      "end": 623.26,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "And it would just get cut here."
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 625.77,
      "end": 628.805,
      "duration": 3.035,
      "text": "I would call such a thing a partial digestion."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 632.21,
      "end": 634.81,
      "duration": 2.6,
      "text": "It can be done one of two ways."
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 634.81,
      "end": 637.38,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "I could just add a little bit of restriction enzyme and not"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 637.38,
      "end": 638.63,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "give it too long."
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 638.63,
      "end": 640.8,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "Or I could add a mixture of a little restriction enzyme, a"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 640.8,
      "end": 643.73,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "little methylation enzyme, and let them have at it."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 643.73,
      "end": 646.54,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "And if I had the right balance, I could cut on"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 646.54,
      "end": 650.73,
      "duration": 4.19,
      "text": "average every second restriction site or on average"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 650.73,
      "end": 652.88,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "every fourth restriction site."
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 652.88,
      "end": 656.97,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "Or if I use a different ratio, every tenth restriction site."
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 656.97,
      "end": 660.382,
      "duration": 3.412,
      "text": "So I actually can play a stochastic, a probabilistic"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 660.382,
      "end": 665.49,
      "duration": 5.108,
      "text": "game of cutting every second, fourth, tenth site and"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 665.49,
      "end": 666.42,
      "duration": 0.93,
      "text": "obviously get a mix."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 666.42,
      "end": 668.25,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "I'll get a mixture of different cuts."
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 668.25,
      "end": 671.45,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "But in terms of cutting in the middle of my gene, I no longer"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 671.45,
      "end": 675.01,
      "duration": 3.56,
      "text": "care because I can do partial digestions."
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 675.01,
      "end": 678.13,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "Now that means that in my library I might not just have"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 678.13,
      "end": 679.27,
      "duration": 1.14,
      "text": "the Eco fragments."
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 679.27,
      "end": 681.82,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "But because I did a partial digestion, I might have two"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 681.82,
      "end": 684.13,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "consecutive or five consecutive Eco fragments, if"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 684.13,
      "end": 685.7,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "I've done a partial digestion."
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 685.7,
      "end": 686.86,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "But your question still stands."
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 686.86,
      "end": 689.74,
      "duration": 2.88,
      "text": "How do I find my right gene?"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 689.74,
      "end": 691.64,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "How do I figure out which is the right gene?"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 695.69,
      "end": 698.43,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "So I've got this."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 698.43,
      "end": 699.68,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "I've got my plate."
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 702.04,
      "end": 704.82,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "I've done this amazing purification."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 704.82,
      "end": 709.32,
      "duration": 4.5,
      "text": "Every one of these guys has a chunk of human DNA that might"
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 709.32,
      "end": 711.09,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "be just one EcoR1 fragment."
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 711.09,
      "end": 714.43,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "Or if I happen to have done a partial digestion, it might be"
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 714.43,
      "end": 716.45,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "two EcoR1 fragments."
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 716.45,
      "end": 724.262,
      "duration": 7.812,
      "text": "But it turns out that this guy here is beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 724.262,
      "end": 725.97,
      "duration": 1.708,
      "text": "How do I know?"
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 725.97,
      "end": 727.05,
      "duration": 1.08,
      "text": "I've purified beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 727.05,
      "end": 728.43,
      "duration": 1.38,
      "text": "I get points, right?"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 728.43,
      "end": 730.07,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "I purified beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 730.07,
      "end": 731.93,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "Somewhere on my plate is a pure"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 731.93,
      "end": 734.52,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "beta-globin sitting there."
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 734.52,
      "end": 738.18,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "But the problem is I don't know where it is."
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 738.18,
      "end": 739.89,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "How am I going to find it?"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 739.89,
      "end": 741.08,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "They all still look the same."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 741.08,
      "end": 742.33,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "They look like bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 745.867,
      "end": 747.791,
      "duration": 1.924,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 747.791,
      "end": 749.864,
      "duration": 2.073,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: To do what?"
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 749.864,
      "end": 753.343,
      "duration": 3.479,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Well, in this case find some way to determine"
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 753.343,
      "end": 757.33,
      "duration": 3.987,
      "text": "whether or not a certain certain has beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 757.33,
      "end": 758.3,
      "duration": 0.97,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Whether a certain colony--"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 758.3,
      "end": 759.5,
      "duration": 1.2,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Has beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 759.5,
      "end": 761.61,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Has the beta-globin gene in it."
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 761.61,
      "end": 765.33,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "So I somehow have to test each colony to figure out whether"
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 765.33,
      "end": 766.78,
      "duration": 1.45,
      "text": "it's got the beta-globin gene in it."
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 766.78,
      "end": 768.07,
      "duration": 1.29,
      "text": "How do you propose to do that?"
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 772.84,
      "end": 774.09,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: There's some observation you can make."
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 778.13,
      "end": 778.605,
      "duration": 0.475,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Talk loud."
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 778.605,
      "end": 781.16,
      "duration": 2.555,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: There's some observation you can make."
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 781.16,
      "end": 782.91,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: And you make that observation."
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 782.91,
      "end": 785.46,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "Right, so--"
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 785.46,
      "end": 785.96,
      "duration": 0.5,
      "text": "I'm with you."
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 785.96,
      "end": 786.918,
      "duration": 0.958,
      "text": "Yeah?"
    },
    {
      "index": 263,
      "start": 786.918,
      "end": 789.313,
      "duration": 2.395,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: You basically want some ribosomes"
    },
    {
      "index": 264,
      "start": 789.313,
      "end": 790.75,
      "duration": 1.437,
      "text": "to create the proteins."
    },
    {
      "index": 265,
      "start": 790.75,
      "end": 792.87,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Oh, oh, oh, so maybe I can make that thing"
    },
    {
      "index": 266,
      "start": 792.87,
      "end": 794.86,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "make beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 267,
      "start": 794.86,
      "end": 797.19,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "Oh, and then look for the protein."
    },
    {
      "index": 268,
      "start": 797.19,
      "end": 798.96,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "Problem with that is E.coli doesn't read human"
    },
    {
      "index": 269,
      "start": 798.96,
      "end": 800.36,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "instructions."
    },
    {
      "index": 270,
      "start": 800.36,
      "end": 802.03,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "So E.coli's polymerase won't read."
    },
    {
      "index": 271,
      "start": 802.03,
      "end": 802.96,
      "duration": 0.93,
      "text": "But it's a great idea."
    },
    {
      "index": 272,
      "start": 802.96,
      "end": 803.94,
      "duration": 0.98,
      "text": "Maybe we can do that."
    },
    {
      "index": 273,
      "start": 803.94,
      "end": 805.59,
      "duration": 1.65,
      "text": "Any other ideas?"
    },
    {
      "index": 274,
      "start": 805.59,
      "end": 807.36,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "How are we going to find our gene?"
    },
    {
      "index": 275,
      "start": 807.36,
      "end": 808.41,
      "duration": 1.05,
      "text": "We've made a library."
    },
    {
      "index": 276,
      "start": 808.41,
      "end": 809.1,
      "duration": 0.69,
      "text": "We have a library."
    },
    {
      "index": 277,
      "start": 809.1,
      "end": 810.79,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "It's a bigger library than MIT."
    },
    {
      "index": 278,
      "start": 810.79,
      "end": 812.63,
      "duration": 1.84,
      "text": "It's got more volumes than MIT."
    },
    {
      "index": 279,
      "start": 812.63,
      "end": 813.98,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "How are we're going to find our book?"
    },
    {
      "index": 280,
      "start": 813.98,
      "end": 816.82,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: Put it in a medium without beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 281,
      "start": 816.82,
      "end": 819.932,
      "duration": 3.112,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Put a medium without beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 282,
      "start": 819.932,
      "end": 820.9,
      "duration": 0.968,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: See if it grows or not."
    },
    {
      "index": 283,
      "start": 820.9,
      "end": 823.39,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: See if it grows up."
    },
    {
      "index": 284,
      "start": 823.39,
      "end": 825.7,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "E.coli couldn't care less about beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 285,
      "start": 825.7,
      "end": 826.8,
      "duration": 1.1,
      "text": "It doesn't need beta-globin."
    },
    {
      "index": 286,
      "start": 826.8,
      "end": 829.06,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "And in addition, it won't produce beta-globin because it"
    },
    {
      "index": 287,
      "start": 829.06,
      "end": 831.48,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "doesn't read the human instructions."
    },
    {
      "index": 288,
      "start": 831.48,
      "end": 833.96,
      "duration": 2.48,
      "text": "All right, so we've gone to all this trouble."
    },
    {
      "index": 289,
      "start": 833.96,
      "end": 837.68,
      "duration": 3.72,
      "text": "We've made a library with all the possible books in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 290,
      "start": 837.68,
      "end": 839.38,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "human genome."
    },
    {
      "index": 291,
      "start": 839.38,
      "end": 841.17,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "And we don't know how to use the library."
    },
    {
      "index": 292,
      "start": 844.48,
      "end": 847.19,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "Friday's lecture let us discuss"
    },
    {
      "index": 293,
      "start": 847.19,
      "end": 848.44,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "how to use the library."
    }
